\section{Overview}

As a subject of a research a simple robot will be taken, with two grippers 
and an elbow joint that can manipulate blocks (cuboctahedral voxels) one at a time.
An experimental platform will be realised as a simulation in Gazebo environment 
with control from ROS2 nodes. The  blocks and environment geometry robot joints 
and sensors and conections will be defined in Xacro/URDF files. 

Analysis of R in R + M + E:

1. Control system (algorithm)
2. Robot structure (geometry, kinematic reachability)
3. Robot+Environmental reachability checking

Robot configurations synthesis for some objective function
(defined reachability or for defined environment)

1. Kinematic robot configuration checking

Search of the optimal robot configuration for defined environment.
Create a set of configurations combining blocks: 3,4,5,6,7 of different types ()
Model check reachability of some field (e.g.+-1) for each configuration

Advantage: optimal configuration for a new robot

2. Model checking of a overall system (control+robot-configuration+

3. Counterexample based pathfinding in-place assembly

4. Counterexample based pathfinding in local space

